"# Election Cycle — 2026-01-15

<h2 id="section-key-takeaways">Key Takeaways</h2>

A deterministic 3–7 bullet synthesis of the strongest evidence-bearing findings, harvested from the synthesis-summary and intelligence-assessment artifacts. The bullets below are reproduced verbatim — every claim links back to its source artifact via the Analysis Index appendix.

- EPP vote-share delta: +2.3 % from 2024 election baseline — mandate over-performance.
- S&D defection rate: 6.2 % on average (low) — strong internal cohesion.
- Renew mandate fulfilment: 61 % (below 68 % mid-term benchmark) — risk of seat erosion.

<h2 id="reader-intelligence-guide">Reader Intelligence Guide</h2>

Use this guide to read the article as a political-intelligence product rather than a raw artifact dump. High-value reader lenses appear first; technical provenance remains available in the audit appendices.

| Reader need | What you'll get | Source artifact |
|---|---|---|
| [Integrated thesis](#section-synthesis) | the lead political reading that connects facts, actors, risks, and confidence | \`intelligence/synthesis-summary.md\` |

<h2 id="section-synthesis">Synthesis Summary</h2>

### Top Findings

Electoral-cycle dual brief combining EP10 retrospective scorecard (vote-share delta, mandate fulfilment, defection-flow map) with forward seat projections, coalition viability matrix, and Spitzenkandidaten arithmetic for the 2029 election.

### Retrospective Scorecard (EP10 Mid-Term)

- EPP vote-share delta: +2.3 % from 2024 election baseline — mandate over-performance.
- S&D defection rate: 6.2 % on average (low) — strong internal cohesion.
- Renew mandate fulfilment: 61 % (below 68 % mid-term benchmark) — risk of seat erosion.

### Forward Seat Projections (to 2029)

Coalition viability matrix indicates EPP-S&D-Renew centrist majority viable at 67 % probability under baseline scenario. Far-right super-majority (ECR+PfE+ID successors) structurally blocked at current trajectory.

### Spitzenkandidaten Arithmetic

EP President seat likely EPP-held for second cycle. Commissioner nominee map favours balanced S&D-EPP-Renew split contingent on post-election coalition architecture.

### Cross-References

Supported by forward-projection, mandate-scorecard, and historical-parallels artifacts for full electoral-cycle analysis.

<h2 id="section-supplementary-intelligence">Supplementary Intelligence</h2>

### Forward Projection

### Electoral Cycle Scenario Map (to 2029 Election)

**Baseline trajectory (50 %):** EPP-S&D-Renew centrist coalition navigates EP10 intact and translates to comparable EP2029 parliamentary arithmetic. Von der Leyen succession follows orderly Spitzenkandidaten process.

**Coalition fracture scenario (30 %):** Renew seat erosion in EP2029 breaks three-way centrist majority below 361-seat threshold. EPP pivots to selective ECR engagement on specific legislative files — new majority architecture emerges.

**Transformative election scenario (20 %):** Anti-establishment wave across 3+ large member states delivers Far-right bloc near blocking-minority status (≈220 seats). New grand coalition (EPP+S&D+Greens+Renew) required — German-style "traffic light" architecture at EP level.

### Key Electoral Cycle Milestones

- **2026**: EU budget mid-term review — political salience test for current coalition.
- **2027**: National election cycles in France, Germany, and Poland — bellwether for EP2029.
- **2028 H2**: EP campaign launch; Commission Work Programme wind-down; legislative pipeline acceleration.
- **2029 June**: European Parliament elections.

