"# Year Ahead — 2026-01-15

<h2 id="section-key-takeaways">Key Takeaways</h2>

A deterministic 3–7 bullet synthesis of the strongest evidence-bearing findings, harvested from the synthesis-summary and intelligence-assessment artifacts. The bullets below are reproduced verbatim — every claim links back to its source artifact via the Analysis Index appendix.

- **Presidency transition (July)**: Polish-to-Danish handover introduces 6-week agenda discontinuity.
- **AI Act delegation window**: Three delegated acts due by September — EP scrutiny rights activated.
- **Defence Fund**: Disbursement conditionality debate likely to resurface in Q3 budget discussions.

<h2 id="reader-intelligence-guide">Reader Intelligence Guide</h2>

Use this guide to read the article as a political-intelligence product rather than a raw artifact dump. High-value reader lenses appear first; technical provenance remains available in the audit appendices.

| Reader need | What you'll get | Source artifact |
|---|---|---|
| [Integrated thesis](#section-synthesis) | the lead political reading that connects facts, actors, risks, and confidence | \`intelligence/synthesis-summary.md\` |

<h2 id="section-synthesis">Synthesis Summary</h2>

### Top Findings

EP annual strategic outlook for 2026 covers Commission Work Programme delivery, Trio Presidency (Poland/Denmark/Cyprus) transition, and 12-month legislative pipeline priorities spanning climate, digital, and defence.

### Annual Strategic Outlook

The 12-month legislative horizon carries four flagship trilogues near conclusion: CBAM implementation acts, Defence Fund regulation, AI Act delegated acts, and Digital Networks Act. Each carries coalition risk above baseline.

### Strategic Risk Surfaces

- **Presidency transition (July)**: Polish-to-Danish handover introduces 6-week agenda discontinuity.
- **AI Act delegation window**: Three delegated acts due by September — EP scrutiny rights activated.
- **Defence Fund**: Disbursement conditionality debate likely to resurface in Q3 budget discussions.

### Cross-References

Supported by forward-projection artifact covering 12-month scenario analysis.

<h2 id="section-supplementary-intelligence">Supplementary Intelligence</h2>

### Forward Projection

### 12-Month Scenario Map

**Baseline scenario (55 %):** EP legislative programme delivers Commission Work Programme 2026 core priorities. Trio Presidency (Poland → Denmark → Cyprus) maintains institutional continuity. No snap elections or major coalition realignment.

**Upside scenario (25 %):** Defence Fund disbursement accelerates; AI Act delegated acts adopted on schedule; CBAM phase-in completes without third-country retaliation. EP-Commission co-legislative momentum highest in EP10 term.

**Downside scenario (20 %):** US-EU trade dispute escalation triggers EP emergency procedures, displacing planned legislative calendar. Geopolitical shock (Ukraine ceasefire collapse) forces budget re-prioritisation.

### 12-Month Forward Indicators

- Plenary sessions: 12 scheduled (monthly Strasbourg + Brussels supplementary sessions).
- Flagship trilogues: 4 near-conclusion, 6 in active negotiation, 3 mandate phase.
- Presidency handovers: 2 (Poland → Denmark July, Denmark → Cyprus December).

